{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Mechanism-ratchet archaeology (2026-09-06): design-free-fixable. The sanctioned path is already marker-only: `scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py` says `--check` exits 0 when every new/increased mechanism carries a non-blank exact-key `# mechanism-ok:` marker; `scripts/_mechanism_delta/compare.py:evaluate()` partitions new/increased keys into admitted/unadmitted using the marker map and returns 0 when only admitted regressions remain. `docs/architecture.md` §Mechanism-delta ratchet says `--update-stale` is maintenance-only and the contributor path is the marker or removing the mechanism.\n\nThe two unit-test invariants now pin that same contract: `tests/unit/test_mechanism_delta.py::test_check_passes_on_the_committed_tree` accepts either `new=0` or `admitted`, and `test_the_committed_baseline_matches_the_live_tree` asserts `set(baseline) | admitted == live`. A source-level regression test at lines ~480-530 exists specifically because the marker-honouring assertions were once lost in a wholesale revert; it states that otherwise a correct marker fails the suite and hand-editing the baseline is the forbidden fallback.\n\nConclusion: making marker green imply tests green is a defect fix in the existing sanctioned path, not a new exception/bypass mechanism. No user design decision is needed unless an implementation proposes something other than exact-key marker admission + diagnostics for unmatched/miskeyed markers."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788763482506937001,"uuid":"9cebfe5f-79a9-40fb-ac89-6f27eee7446f"}